{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/627199-homebrew-new-numina-house-ruled-numina","id":627199,"title":"[Homebrew] New Numina + House Ruled Numina","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-14T20:52:24-07:00","id":627199,"title":"[Homebrew] New Numina + House Ruled Numina","content":"All feedback is welcome. I noticed how no official Numen I've seen thus far requires the expenditure of a Willpower point. So I decided to house rule that spending extra Essence and/or 1 Willpower point is permitted for certain Numina. This usually increases the duration/range/precision of the effect.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">General Considerations</span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The limit for effective successes of an entity that must be reached or surpassed to contest a Numen/Influence is [Rank], even if the entity got [Rank + X] successes. In other words, if the entity has Rank 3 and gets 5 successes, those contesting it only need to get 3 successes. If they get 2 or fewer, the entity is still considered to have gained an Exceptional Success.<br /> <br /> Of note is that there is no limit for the effective success of monsters that are not ephemeral beings. This is due to the fact that ephemeral beings can accumulate gigantic dice pools very fast, and they receive bonus godlike success for rolls related to their purview at Rank 6+. The normally playable templates, on the other hand, are usually limited to a dice pool of around 15-20, and they don't get bonus godlike successes when they have Blood Potency/Primal Urge/Gnosis 6+.<br /> <br /> I am aware that all of this makes Rank 6+ entities less godlike, but you are not obligated to use these guidelines for every PC and NPC, all the time. You may use them selectively and alter the numbers. Do whatever works best for your group.<br /> <br /> Have a new Merit that is likewise meant to improve the protective measures of mortals against supernatural powers:<br /> <br /> <b>Unyielding (5 Dots):</b> Your character may spend 1 willpower point to double her Resolve, Composure or Stamina when applying it as a penalty to any supernatural powers that alter thought, emotion or body. He may also spend 1 willpower point to the gain the 8 Again benefit on contested rolls against such powers. The Tolerance granted by his Conviction still applies. This Merit stacks with Indomitable. Prerequisites: No Supernatural Template, Conviction 4 or 5 (Or all Resistance Attributes at 3+ if you don't include Conviction)<br /> <br /> The rules for the Conviction Powerstat may be found on the &quot;Mirrors&quot; supplement for 1ed NWOD, pages 32 to 35.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">New Optional Tilt</span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><i>Enfeebled</i> </b></span><br /> <br /> The ephemeral being has been significantly weakened by certain Relics, occult rituals or devices of unorthodox science.<br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> The ephemeral being loses all Willpower points and cannot regain any while the Tilt lasts. Additionally, the item or method that inflicts this Tilt may halve the dice pools of one or two of the following: Numina, Manifestations and Influences. Should the ST allow and item or method that halves the dice pool of all three, it should be limited to one use before losing the capacity to inflict this Til (other powers may remain). Even if someone wants to be affected by these 3 types of powers or the ephemeral being is targeting something inanimate, the Tilt still applies. Mundane uses of Attribute + Attribute and Rank-As-Skill retain their normal dice pools.<br /> <br /> <b>Causing The Tilt:</b> Certain Relics may have the capacity to Enfeeble as an explicit power. They are usually limited to beings from the 4 main types of ephemeral being (Angel/Ghost/Goetic/Spirit) that also have a relatively specific purview, such as car-spirits or messenger angels. The difficulty of using the Relic in question to Enfeeble should be factored into its cost and drawbacks. The more versatile examples only need a successful attack on the ephemeral being. Others might need to hit during certain seasons or cosmological phenomena. Some might even require the ephemeral being to be convinced that the Relic is gift, tribute or the like, and consume or use it as a mundane equivalent is meant to be consumed or used. Other Relics might not inflict this Tilt by themselves, but contain instructions for rituals that might. Unusual scientific devices and inventions are also a valid option. To reiterate: the source of this Tilt does not have to be a Relic or strictly supernatural. Bans and Banes do not inflict this Tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Ending The Tilt:</b> The Tilt can only end when the scene ends.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">New Numina</span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Maim:</b> Spend 3 Essence and roll Power + Finesse vs Stamina + Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance as an instant action against a target within Rank x 3 yards. If a successful Grapple roll consisting of Finesse + Rank \u2013 Defense is made first, the ephemeral being may spend 1 less Essence. No additional penalty for targeting a specific body part is applied. If the ephemeral being gets more successes, inflict the Arm Wrack or Leg Wrack Tilt. This does not cause damage. You may apply cosmetic touches to the affected limb based on the ephemeral being\u2019s purview, such as charred bones for a fire-spirit or tumors for a disease-ridden ghost. The Tilt lasts for a number of turns equal to successes. By spending 5 Essence + 1 Willpower point (no +3 bonus), the Tilt lasts for one hour per success. An Exceptional Success applies the Tilt to both arms OR both legs.<br /> <br /> <b>Plague:</b> Same mechanics as the previous Numen, but it inflicts the Sick or Poisoned Tilt, whichever is more thematically fitting. Cosmetic effects may still be applied. If you spend 5 Essence + 1 Willpower point and also get an Exceptional Success, the Tilt is grave instead of moderate. If the ST continues the effect of the Tilt outside combat, the Toxicity rating is equal to Rank, with damage being dealt each hour. Ephemeral beings of Rank 3+ are normally the ones that can inflict either Tilt, but not always.<br /> <br /> <b>Roar:</b> Spend 2 Essence and roll Power + Resistance vs Stamina + Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance. The ephemeral being unleashes a horribly loud sound that is thematically appropriate. Anyone within Rank x 10 yards who does not get as many successes as the ephemeral being suffers the Deafened Tilt for a number of turns equal to successes. By spending 4 Essence + 1 willpower point, the Tilt lasts for one hour per success. Every additional point of Essence spent increases the radius by 10 yards. Despite the wide radius, this Numen produces real sound, so the appropriate barriers may negate successes or even render it useless. However, the sound does not travel any further than the aforementioned radius, so the ephemeral being does not risk too much unwanted attention.<br /> <br /> <b>Legion:</b> Often referred to with collective nouns suiting the ephemeral being\u2019s purview, this Numen is always active unless suppressed as a reflexive action. The ephemeral being is surrounded by instances of its purview, such as flying insects, floating daggers or spheres of phantom fire. The Legion has a radius of Rank x 3 yards, centered around of the ephemeral being. Those caught within this radius roll Defense - Rank, with Evasion as an optional action. Those that fail the roll suffer 2 bashing damage. This damage may be upgraded to lethal by spending 1 Essence. A single success reduces damage from 2 to 1, while a number of successes equal to the entity's Rank reduces it to 0. Armor does not help unless it covers the entire body and its general rating matches or exceeds the entity's Rank. The entity may specify who will be targeted and who won't, without additional rolls nor Essence expenditure. (Note: If you want the ephemeral being to cause dice penalties instead of damage within a field of effect, use the Emotional Aura Numen, house ruled below).</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">House Ruled Numina</span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Emotional Aura:</b> The radius is increased to Rank x 5. The penalty is no longer a fixed -2. Each success on the Power + Finesse roll inflicts a -1 penalty (up to -5). This Numen now costs 2 Essence.<br /> <br /> <b>Innocuous:</b> The ephemeral being gains 9 Again when rolling Finesse + Rank for the purposes of stealth.<br /> <br /> <b>Mortal Mask:</b> A casual Wits + Composure roll to notice an ephemeral being disguising itself with this Numen suffers a penalty equal to Finesse/2 round down, rather than Finesse. The Perception roll to see flaws in the disguise can be more thorough, usually consisting of Wits + Skill. Said Skill might be Investigation/Occult to look for tiny marks of the entity\u2019s purview, Medicine to notice flawed anatomy, Empathy for strange mannerisms, and so on. This Perception roll is penalized by the successes of the Power + Finesse roll (up to -5). Characters able to sense the entity in Twilight do not suffer penalties to Perception rolls, as before..<br /> <br /> <b>Telekinesis:</b> Fine motor control is possible with this Numen. Spend 1 Essence and roll Finesse + Resistance reflexively. Successes become the \u201cDexterity\u201d for careful handling. Whether the ephemeral being is using \u201cStrength\u201d or \u201cDexterity\u201d, add Rank to represent the relevant Skill. Targets still use Defense and may Dodge, as if the object was being thrown normally. After the object is released or thrown, the corresponding roll and Essence expenditure must be repeated. However, the extremely fine motor control displayed by sophisticated machines or supernatural powers meant for great precision is still impossible. The maximum Size of the object is equal to Power or Resistance, whichever is higher.<br /> <br /> <b>Awe:</b> The affected targets may still benefit from Defense and Dodging. Those looking at the ephemeral being may substitute Presence with Resolve if they wish.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-23-2015, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T21:10:41-07:00","id":627220,"title":"","content":"I decided to post some other homebrewed Numina I had lying around.<br /> <br /> <b>Ravage:</b> Power + Rank rolls for melee attacks deal +0L by default. Every 2 Essence spent increases the Damage Bonus by 1 for the scene. Your maximum Damage Bonus is equal to [Rank]. Apply the target's Defense and Armor. Each point of Damage Bonus above +5L becomes 1 point of Armor Piercing.<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis:</b> Every 3 Essence spent gives 1/1 Armor for one scene. You may gain up to [Rank/Rank] Armor with this Numen. Each 1/1 Armor above 5/5 does not remove 1 success, but cancels Armor Piercing on a 1 for 1 ratio.<br /> <br /> <b>Mirage:</b> This Numen requires 2 Essence per turn. The ephemeral being's Corpus turns blurry, chaotic or otherwise confusing, allowing it to apply its Defense against long range attacks for one turn, such as Firearms and the Blast Numen. Each individual attacking it after the first, regardless of dice pool, imposes a cumulative -1 on the being's Defense, as before. <br /> <br /> <b>Soul Sight:</b> Roll Finesse + Rank as an instant action. Success allows you to interpret the body language and aura of the target to gain information about him. First use of this Numen in the scene is free, but each subsequent use within the scene costs 2 Essence. Clash Of Wills may happen if the target is actively trying to conceal his thoughts, emotions or aura. Each success allows the ephemeral being to ask an equal or lower number of questions. Successes that exceed the entity's Rank are not considered. Be mindful of what the ephemeral being's purview is, as that guides what questions it probably makes and how its senses interpret the visions. Sample questions below, taken from the Aura Sight Technology and 2ed Auspex:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">* What is this person's mood? A flash of emotion on the victim's face. Ideas normally alien to the ephemeral come flooding into its senses.<br /> <br /> * What is this person afraid of right now? A spark of terror in the victim's eyes. Thoughts of pain or suspicions of being discovered.<br /> <br /> * What is this person's Vice or one of his Aspirations? A hidden smile over a guilty pleasure. Impressions of a faraway person or building.<br /> <br /> * Is this person being controlled by someone else? Eyes shifting around looking for their master. Colored threads leading away from the person.<br /> <br /> * Is this person a supernatural creature -- and if I have seen them before, what is she? Dark threads surrounding a vampire. Wire cables coming off of a demon.<br /> <br /> * Who here does this person want to hurt most? Glances towards the intended victim.<br /> <br /> * Who here is the most likely to give me what I want? Blood throbbing through the victim\u2019s jugular vein. The sound of jingling coins from the victim\u2019s pocket.<br /> <br /> * Who/what here is most likely to lapse into violence? The victim\u2019s hands stained with blood. The smell of gunpowder wafting from the victim.<br /> <br /> * Who here is most afraid? The smell of urine from the victim\u2019s pants. A whimpering sound from the victim.<br /> <br /> * Who/what here is most likely to hurt me? Blood drying on a car crusher. Waves of hot rage boiling off the victim.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-21-2015, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T22:29:26-07:00","id":627274,"title":"","content":"They seem legit, though I'm sleepy, so not thinking straight now.<br /> <br /> What I can say for sure is that Maim and Plague should let Resisted Rolls. First because effects that don't graduate with successes usually ask for Resisted Roll. Second because all Tilts they can inflict seem clearly to ask for Stamina. Maybe Stamina + Dexterity + Supernatural Tolerance, or Stamina + Armor + Supernatural Tolerance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T16:45:53-07:00","id":629171,"title":"","content":"I made significant revisions to the original post's Numina, according to Monteparnas' advice. I also added guidelines for game balance regarding supernatural powers and a new Tilt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T06:43:36-07:00","id":629857,"title":"","content":"New considerations, now with proper sleep.<br /> <br /> The &quot;General Considerations&quot; section is a bit confusing. I do find the rules in there too hard on the ephemeral beings, and the bonuses for Exceptional Success in resistance too large. But regardless of opinion, I had to reread the section two times to be sure that I understood. It needs clarification, maybe identifying better each piece of rule and separating them. The idea of making such exceptional defenses as Merits isn't a bad one.<br /> <br /> I liked the <i>Enfeebled</i> Tilt's idea, but it is harsh, though. That can difficult its use, because it makes any relic so prepared too powerful against a great variation of spirits, and the ST becomes limited to either make hugely powerful entities, or find ways to circumvent the Relic, making it useless. Maybe a good idea could be to break the Tilt in minor ones, with the possibility for a Relic to have any combination of them and its own rules about how to deliver each. That way an ST can fine-tune the use of the Tilts for her chronicle.<br /> <br /> For the new Numina, <b>Maim</b> and <b>Plague</b> are good, I liked 'em. But I would change two things. First, remove the touch necessity. This is the supernatural power of a spiritual entity, it both deserves to be powerful and have to be worth the cost in Essence and Action. The resistance roll is already very good, specially if your general rules are applied. Would also remove the limit of once per target, it seems unnecessary. The most a spirit can achieve repeatedly attacking with such powers the same target is to deplete quickly their own reserves.<br /> <br /> <b>Roar</b> seems ok for me, maybe just add an option to spend more Essence for a wider radius. +1 Essence for +10 yards, maybe? <b>Legion</b> is great, but could be tweaked a little: instead of the entity rolling for attack against each target, it would make more sense for the targets to roll Defense - Rank, with Evasion as an optional action. A single success reduces damage from 2 to 1, while a number of successes equal the entity's Rank reduces it to 0. And with that, your General Rules would be able to be applied to this Numen (since it isn't a direct attack, it seems fair).<br /> <br /> With the house-ruled Numina, <b>Emotional Aura</b> and <b>Innocuous</b> are well done. <b>Mortal Mask</b> I think if Rank wouldn't be a better penalty than successes, but nothing against not using pure Finesse. Maybe Finesse could be used for casual observation and Rank or Successes for thoroughly examination. I didn't get <b>Telekinesis</b>, though. You put a greater cost for the purpose of making it able to handle fine movement, but this same advantage is negated and the Numen seems to do exactly the same thing, just with more rules and unnecessary limitations. Awe also seems to not need such limitations.<br /> <br /> Going to the second bath of new Numina, <b>Ravage</b> and <b>Aegis</b> are very good. <b>Mirage</b> seems too encumbered with rules for limitations. Given that it is just a turn of benefit, 2 Essence could be the only cost, without any roll. <b>Soul Sight</b> could be a little stronger, maybe giving away as much information as the number of successes (like 2nd level Auspex), or simply enabling the entity to repeat it at will (and depleting its resources with such), but overall seems very good.<br /> <br /> Most of the Numina and modifications seems legit and indeed good ideas, but you seem over-preoccupied with balance, to the point of being too conservative. Balance is <u>almost</u> a non-issue with ephemeral beings, and you already presented good weapons against them with your new rules and the Tilt. With too much concern about the effects on game of powerful high-ranking entities, you're taxing too much the low-ranking ones, and those are the ones more used. Most of your Numina are already limited by Essence cost, sometimes higher than necessary. It should remain your main source of limits for Numina, because it is what will keep entities from fighting and weaker them in a more thoroughly manner. Lessening the power of a Numen only makes it less useful, and a less interesting combat option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T15:46:27-07:00","id":635113,"title":"","content":"Thank you once more for your excellent feedback, Monteparnas. I did my best to use all of it. And yes, now that you have pointed it out, it does seem clear that I'm too worried about game balance in several ways. I'll try to be less nervous about this in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T09:38:11-07:00","id":635924,"title":"","content":"Be welcome.<br /> <br /> And you can bring more material if you want. The current one is so good that I will actually translate it to Portuguese right now and post at a Brazilian forum, as much to show it to my friends and to have it at hand when I want to use it myself (because I will, maybe soon).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T17:34:34-07:00","id":636480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/627199-homebrew-new-numina-house-ruled-numina?p=635924#post635924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Be welcome.<br /> <br /> And you can bring more material if you want. The current one is so good that I will actually translate it to Portuguese right now and post at a Brazilian forum, as much to show it to my friends and to have it at hand when I want to use it myself (because I will, maybe soon).</div> </div> </div> </div> Really? That's awesome! I am actually Brazilian myself. Could you send me the translations via private message so I can help with them? You can send the message in Portuguese, if you prefer.<br /> <br /> Also, have another 3 original Numina. I noticed how there were no options for ephemeral beings whose purview was not strictly animal related to transform into animals. That's a borderline ubiquitous power for spirits and gods in real life mythology. Weather controlling powers not covered by Influences were also absent. Lastly, another near omnipresent power in mythology was not included: having demigod offspring with humans and animals.<br /> <br /> There were also no Manifestations for entering the Hedge or Astral Realms, but I'll wait for more 2ed open dev posts about Mage/Changeling/Beast before deciding if I'll homebrew such Manifestations.<br /> <br /> <b>Animal Mask:</b> This Numen disguises a Materialized entity as animal and can be used at the same time as the Materialize Manifestation. Using this Numen costs 1 Essence and the transformation lasts for activation successes in hours. The flaws in this disguise and the penalties it inflicts to Perception rolls are covered in the house rules for the Mortal Mask Numen. Characters able to sense the entity in Twilight do not suffer penalties to Perception rolls, as before. The types of animals that are symbolically and/or metaphorically associated with its purview. A night-spirit might turn into a bat or owl, but a guardian angel probably won't turn into an ant. The amount of animal types that an ephemeral being can transform into is usually limited to Rank, with one type being added or subtracted if you want. The ephemeral being can communicate using both the animal's inherent capabilities, and with a human voice. Manifestations, Numina and Influences still work, unless determined otherwise by context. For a list of stats for several animals, <a href=\"http://nwod.org/wiki/index.php/Bestiary\" target=\"_blank\"><b>read this</b></a> (some also updated to 2ed rules in <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/140729-new-animal-stats\">this thread</a></b>). The ephemeral being keeps its stats: those links are there mostly for illustrative purposes.<br /> <br /> <b>Weather Control:</b> The ephemeral entity may inflict an Environmental Tilt related to its purview once per scene by spending 7 Essence and rolling Power + Finesse. Cosmetic effects based on purview are permitted. By Spending an additional 5 Essence + 1 willpower point, the entity can apply an unusual secondary effect to the Tilt and also specify who will be affected and won't. Examples of additional effects include a Flood made of any bodily fluid or combination thereof, or a strangely colored Inferno that is removed by something other than water or a fire extinguisher. This Tilt applies for the rest of the scene and is relatively localized. A good rule of thumb is a radius of Rank x 100 yards. Each 2 points of additional Essence spent increases the radius by 100 yards. The intensity of the Tilt, if it must be specified, is equal to the ephemeral being's successes on the Power + Finesse roll (up to Rank). This Numen is the mark of powerful entities. An entity below Rank 5 possessing this Numen is exceedingly rare. Entities with a Rank below 5 using this Numen have a radius of Rank x 20 yards, cannot give secondary benefits to the Tilt, the maximum intensity of the Tilt is Rank - 1 and each 2 additional Essence spent only increases the radius by 20 yards.<br /> <br /> <b>Conception:</b> The entity is capable of siring or bearing functional offspring while disguised as a human or animal. The frequent portrayals of this Numen in several mythologies are a huge overestimation of how many entities can really do this. This Numen requires the entity to spend [Rank x 5] Essence to place a sign on the target, which must be directly perceived and within Rank x 10 yards. If the entity has Rank 6+, it cannot send Royal Avatars to do it. The entity must be using the Mortal Mask or Animal Mask Numen. The entity only rolls it unmodified Power to charm the target and to alter probabilities in the favor of seduction. Use the normal rules for Social Maneuvering. The entity must remove all Doors in [Rank] rolls or less. If the entity fails, the Doors are restored and the spent Essence is lost. If it succeeds, all spent Essence is regained, plus 10 Essence and 1 willpower point. An Exceptional Success in the last Social Maneuvering roll results in a child being conceived. The Mortal Mask or Animal Mask Numina last longer to accommodate pregnancy at no additional cost.<br /> <br /> The entities that sire or bear children this way can transfer Essence points remotely to their children reflexively. The child has the same Maximum Essence/Per Turn of the supernatural parent, and can spend this Essence to boost his or her Attributes like an ephemeral being would. Essence is applied to each one of the 9 Material Attributes separately, with the limit of Rank + 2 still applying. The child can spend 1 Essence to heal 1 lethal damage or 2 bashing damage. The supernatural parent often has the <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/626202-new-numina\">Grant Blessing Numen</a></b> and the <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/578026-new-spirit-manifestation-sponsorship\">Sponsorship Manifestation</a></b>. Neither of these powers requires the supernatural parent to be physically present. If the child is Sponsored, each success on a Resonant roll gives 2 Essence to the supernatural parent.<br /> <br /> Once per scene, the supernatural parent may spend 1 willpower point and roll Finesse + Rank to remotely perceive the child\u2019s immediate surroundings for one turn per success with all of its senses, even if the child is inside an Invisible Realm (Hedge, Shadow, Astral, Underworld). If the parent has Rank 6+, the child may spend 1 willpower point to get a number of bonus godlike successes on a Resonant roll equal to the parent\u2019s [Rank/2 round up]. He/she may also receive a number of Numina equal to his/her [Willpower/2 round up] via the parent\u2019s Grant Blessing Numen. Should the child develop a supernatural template of his or her own, the parent can no longer transfer Essence to the child nor use Grant Blessing/Sponsorship remotely. The parent may still spend willpower points to see the child\u2019s surroundings as previously described. Of note is that the supernatural parent does not have to be of Rank 5+ nor a true ephemeral being. The amount of details in the narration for the Social Maneuvering is left up to the game group\u2019s standards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-27-2015, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T23:56:17-07:00","id":636767,"title":"","content":"I'm quite surprised! And I'll be sending the translation through PM, yes. It takes some time to do a translation.<br /> <br /> Now, I doubt that they will do much effort to mix ephemeral beings and their realms. By current rules, they need a Numen even to simply perceive one another at Twilight if not of the same realm. The distinction between realms seems to be a very strong one, something that can only be broken by magic from the Material Realm.<br /> <br /> <b>Animal Mask</b> can be safely locked in the same cost in Essence as <b>Mortal Mask</b>, since the actual animal form is just a mask. It is a little worse by being of less utility than a person disguise, but also a little better for being harder to perceive throw (people pay less attention and have less of a chance to perceive flaws in an animal disguise). Even them, people should have some chance to perceive there's something odd with the animal (actually notice that an animal isn't quite what it seems to be is also a common trope). I can easily see this Numen being more common than <b>Mortal Mask</b>, but I think the devs thought <b>Materialize</b> to be enough. Or, on second thought, you could make this a secondary effect of <b>Mortal Mask</b> by paying +2 Essence and 1 WP.<br /> <br /> <b>Weather Control</b> could use more tweaks. I think that the power to make secondary effects should be more reliable, to begin with. Maybe get rid of the WP cost for the base effect, but you can have the Secondary Effect with +5 Essence (for a huge 12 total!) and 1 WP. An Exceptional Success actually reduces the cost of both base and additional effect by 2 each, making the power much more powerful for entities with the actual Dice Pools to be relatively reliable on Exceptional Successes.<br /> <br /> <b>Conception</b> doesn't need such harsh rules. In fact, it shouldn't have them. Any being inclined to spend a huge amount of Essence and dots of Willpower on top of that aren't going to simply &quot;not bother&quot;. It is quite an investment. Instead, it fits more as simple fluff to <b>Mortal Mask</b> unless you make it have some real return for the entity. You can make it in several ways, but I can think of two general lines of thought right now. One is to make the intercourse somehow benefit the entity. The other is to take benefit of the offspring. Thinking of Zeus, I can think of a powerful Numen that plays with the very Fate of a mortal, but grants the entity fulfillment through both the intercourse and the offspring. Something like a starting investment of Rank x 5 Essence, already quite a sting, to create a marker of Fate on the chosen mortal, one who never had contact with the entity before. Then the entity rolls Power alone to seduce the chosen Mortal in a normal Social Maneuvering. Each roll isn't just the entity acting, but Fate itself turning the world around to make things happen. Even if the mortal gives itself to the entity before, only the final roll counts for the effect. Failure to get the mortal in Rank total rolls means the entity gets nothing and loses the effect. Success means the entity gets the investment back with bonus for a given time. Exceptional Success means a child is conceited, and when it comes to age it will become a supply of Essence itself by its link with the Ephemeral parent. I'm not sure about those rules, but it would give the Numen some raison d'etre. I imagine it being, at lower ranks, the Numen for Succubi and a great variety of folkloric spirits that have sex, and sometimes children, with humans. Gods can reap even more benefits. The child don't need rules itself, unless you want to make them into their own supernatural splat, minor or major (some specific spirits can be able to make unique splats with an advanced use of this Numen, maybe?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T13:37:16-07:00","id":956524,"title":"","content":"Reviving this, because why create a new topic when one exists and is only <i>exactly</i> one year old? <hr />Note: Stuff in [] is questionable and subject to revision. It's just my current thoughts or a placeholder.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Eternal</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The ephemeral being is an unalterable part of the world, able to weather any change and return to its true purpose. Any effect that would alter its fundamental nature (changing its Ban or Bane, rescuplting its personality, increasing or decreasing its Rank) or even \u201cdestroying\u201d (reducing its Corpus and Essence to zero) it, merely cause it to reform the next day exactly as it was. However, the being is also unable to grow beyond its current circumstances. It will never acquire new abilities or higher Rank, though it might gain memories and shift its personality in light of them, somewhat.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shield of Fealty</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The ephemeral being is able to claim ownership and protection over lesser ephemerals under its control, allowing them to use its superior Rank and Attributes for Resistance. If a subordinate ephemeral would be utterly destroyed, their superior can spend 1 Essence of their own to preserve their minion, allowing them to recorporate as normal. [To total number of subordinate beings that can be protected is Rank * Power.]</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gift of Power</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The ephemeral being has the ability to grant its servants the ability to draw upon its power, utilizing its Influence or Numina in place of their own. They pay for the Influence or Numina as if they possessed it, and roll using their own Rank and Attributes for the Dice Pool. An additional point of Essence must paid as a tithe to granting entity\u2019s owner per use (or Scene, if the power is persistent), and is added to the owner's own pool.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Invest Charm</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1+ Essence</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The ephemeral being is able to imbue some of their power into a material object. The being uses one of its Influences, spends Essence, and decides upon a trigger (an event, a keyword, etc.). The Influence is stored in the object and will be activated once the trigger is met, until the object runs out of stored Essence. [An object can store up to Size + Structure safely, with each point over that lowering its Durability by 1.] Essence can be spent to recharge the object on a 1-to-1 basis, as long as it hasn\u2019t been fully depleted.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-23-2016, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T15:18:32-07:00","id":956585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/627199-homebrew-new-numina-house-ruled-numina?p=956524#post956524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Eternal</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The ephemeral being is an unalterable part of the world, able to weather any change and return to its true purpose. Any effect that would alter its fundamental nature (changing its Ban or Bane, rescuplting its personality, increasing or decreasing its Rank) or even \u201cdestroying\u201d (reducing its Corpus and Essence to zero) it, merely cause it to reform the next day exactly as it was. However, the being is also unable to grow beyond its current circumstances. It will never acquire new abilities or higher Rank, though it might gain memories and shift its personality in light of them, somewhat.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank goodness this sort of numina runs counter to everything that Idigam are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}